Create `.claude/hooks/lib/` directory and implement `hook-profiles.js` with:

1. Export `isHookEnabled(hookId, { profiles })` function
2. Read profile from `TEMPLATE_HOOK_PROFILE` env var (default: `standard`)
3. Support `TEMPLATE_DISABLED_HOOKS` for comma-separated hook IDs to disable
4. Define three profiles:
   - `minimal`: session-init, project-index, pre-commit-check, protect-sensitive-files, pre-compact, session-end, pattern-extraction
   - `standard`: adds post-edit-format, console-log-audit, suggest-compact, build-analysis, pr-url-extract, observe
   - `strict`: adds file-size-guard, quality-gate, cost-tracker, typescript-check, doc-file-blocker, dev-server-blocker, long-running-tmux-hint

Pseudo-code:
```javascript
const PROFILES = {
  minimal: ['session-init', 'project-index', 'pre-commit-check', 'protect-sensitive-files', 'pre-compact', 'session-end', 'pattern-extraction'],
  standard: [...minimal, 'post-edit-format', 'console-log-audit', 'suggest-compact', 'build-analysis', 'pr-url-extract', 'observe'],
  strict: [...standard, 'file-size-guard', 'quality-gate', 'cost-tracker', 'typescript-check', 'doc-file-blocker', 'dev-server-blocker', 'long-running-tmux-hint']
};

function isHookEnabled(hookId, options = {}) {
  const profile = process.env.TEMPLATE_HOOK_PROFILE || 'standard';
  const disabledList = (process.env.TEMPLATE_DISABLED_HOOKS || '').split(',').filter(Boolean);

  if (disabledList.includes(hookId)) return false;

  const enabledHooks = PROFILES[profile] || PROFILES.standard;
  return enabledHooks.includes(hookId);
}
```

